## =============================================================================
## deploy/caddy/Caddyfile — the edge: HTTPS, routing, security headers, limits
## =============================================================================
## GUIDE STEP   9.0 (development: the single address http://localhost:8080
##              for the pages and the agent API; the `caddy` service of
##              compose.yml arrives here), 12.3 (production: the e-mail for
##              the certificate authority and HSTS, two lines commented twice)
## PURPOSE      Caddy is the ONLY container reachable from the internet. For
##              every request it:
##                1. terminates TLS in production (decrypts HTTPS;
##                   certificates are obtained and renewed automatically from
##                   Let's Encrypt/ZeroSSL; development uses plain HTTP);
##                2. applies edge rules: body size limit, header timeouts,
##                   per-IP rate limit, security headers;
##                3. forwards the request over the private `edge` network to
##                   the right service:
##                     /mcp*     -> mcp:8000    (MCP server, streaming)
##                     /agent/*  -> agent:8000  (chat API, SSE streaming)
##                     anything  -> web:8000    (Flask: /, /chat, /yaml, /explore, /api/*)
## USED BY      compose.yml service `caddy` (mounted at /etc/caddy/Caddyfile).
## DEPENDS ON   deploy/caddy/Dockerfile (Caddy built with the rate-limit
##              plugin), the variable CADDY_SITE_ADDRESS (set by
##              compose.override.yml in development and by compose.prod.yml
##              from .env in production), DNS record of your domain pointing
##              at the server, ports 80/443 open in the firewall (guide 12.1).
## WHY          Architecture D13 and §6: one entry point (small attack surface),
##              one origin for all components (no CORS needed, cookies work
##              everywhere), TLS configured once, protection from slow clients
##              for the synchronous gunicorn workers, uniform security headers.
## ACTIVATE     9.0: uncomment block by block (the two "Guide 12.3" lines
##              stay commented), then:
##                docker compose run --rm --no-deps caddy caddy validate \
##                    --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
##              (`run` works before Caddy has ever started; while it runs,
##              use `docker compose exec caddy caddy validate ...`.)
##              Done when (9.0): http://localhost:8080/login loads and
##              http://localhost:8080/agent/health answers.
##              12.3: put your real e-mail address in the `email` line,
##              uncomment it and the HSTS line, validate again.
##              Done when (guide 12.3): SSL Labs grade A, and the services are
##              reachable only through Caddy.
## SYNTAX NOTE  In a Caddyfile, `#` starts a comment, so this file follows the
##              same `## ` / `# ` convention as the Python files.
## =============================================================================

## -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
